Kubernetes volumes -
1.empty dir
2.hostpath
3.static provisioning 
4.dynamic provisoning


1. emptyDir

Purpose - Temporary storage shared across containers in a Pod

Lifecycle - Created when the Pod starts, deleted when the Pod stops

Use Cases - inter-container data sharing

Example Use - Shipping the logs from the main container 


2. hostPath

Purpose -Mounts a file/directory from the host node into the Pod

Lifecycle - Lives as long as the data exists on the host

Use Cases - Access to host logs, configuration files


3. Static PV & PVC (Static Provisioning)
Feature Details

PV (PersistentVolume) Manually created volume mapped to pre-existing storage like AWS EBS or NFS

PVC (PersistentVolumeClaim) User-created request that matches the static PV

Lifecycle - Admin provisions PV; user creates PVC to bind

Use Cases - When pre-existing storage resources must be reused


4. Dynamic PV & PVC (Dynamic Provisioning)

Feature - StorageClass Defines how storage is dynamically provisioned

PV & PVC Lifecycle PVC triggers automatic creation of a PV

Use Cases - Scalable, automated environments where storage should be provisioned on-demand

Kubernetes dynamically creates and binds the PV using the StorageClass.
